Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 06:40:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] local patch 2: surface reasoning_text as Anthropic thinking
 blocks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 1 alone left a silent ~5-10K-token loss per response: Copilot's
reasoning-capable models split their output between message.content
(the visible answer) and message.reasoning_text (the chain-of-thought).
The base copilot-api translator only extracts content, so all the CoT
was dropped — yielding short or empty Anthropic responses despite
high output_tokens.

Discovered when testing a 10K-token Python review prompt: the patched
proxy returned output_tokens=8192 but content:[] (empty array). All
8K tokens went to the silently-dropped reasoning_text field.

This patch surfaces reasoning_text and reasoning_opaque on both code
paths:

- Non-streaming (translateToAnthropic): extract message.reasoning_text
  into an Anthropic thinking content block with signature, emitted
  BEFORE text and tool_use blocks per Anthropic ordering convention.

- Streaming (translateChunkToAnthropicEvents): open a thinking content
  block on first delta.reasoning_text, stream thinking_delta events,
  emit signature_delta on delta.reasoning_opaque, and close the
  thinking block when delta.content or delta.tool_calls arrives
  (Anthropic forbids interleaved thinking/text blocks).

Type additions:
- Delta.reasoning_text + Delta.reasoning_opaque (chunk shape)
- ResponseMessage.reasoning_text + .reasoning_opaque (non-stream shape)
- AnthropicThinkingBlock.signature (optional, for the opaque token)
- AnthropicStreamState.thinkingBlockOpen (track open thinking block)

Verified end-to-end via /v1/messages + thinking{budget=64000} on
claude-opus-4.7-1m-internal with a 10K-token review prompt:
  - Streaming: 586 thinking_delta events / 7131 chars CoT
    + 341 text_delta events / 3966 chars answer
    + 1 signature_delta
  - Non-streaming: 20073 chars in text (Copilot inlined this run)

Without this patch, PR review daemons silently lose ~7K chars of
reasoning per turn on long-doc prompts — the typical workload.

See PATCH_NOTES.md for the full 4-layer investigation + before/after
probe numbers.
